<title>ITALY: Mondadori managing director resigns.</title>
<headline>Mondadori managing director resigns.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian publishing group Arnoldo Mondadori Editore Spa said on Tuesday its managing director Paolo Forlin had resigned.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that the company board had called a meeting for February 20.</p>
<p>Forlin, who had been in the position for only six months, was also Vice president of the group.</p>
